# Simple Theme Options — agent conventions (plugin-local mirror)

> **This is the in-plugin mirror of the canonical rules.**
> When the **plugin folder** itself is opened as the Cursor workspace (i.e. someone downloaded only the plugin), this file is the rule Cursor will load. The same content also exists outside the plugin at `wp-content/plugins/simple-theme-options/.cursor/rules/simple-theme-options.mdc` relative to a full WordPress install root (one folder up from `wp-content/`).
>
> **Sync contract:** it does **not** matter which Cursor surface produced the work — **Chat**, **Agent**, **Composer**, or any other prompt tab. Any edit to agent conventions in **either** copy of this rules file **must** be applied to the **other** copy in the **same** assistant turn / change set (never one file only). Paths in this file are written **relative to the plugin root** (i.e. the workspace root when only the plugin is opened). If you are inside a full WordPress install, prepend `wp-content/plugins/simple-theme-options/` to every relative path mentioned below **except** the standalone HTML guide bundle, which lives **outside** the plugin at **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/`** from this plugin root (same as **`<WordPress-root>/docs/simple-theme-options/`**). The companion files that must also be kept in sync are **`README.md`** (plugin root) and that **`docs/simple-theme-options/`** bundle.

When adding or changing options in this plugin, follow these project rules (user-defined).

## Mandatory agent checklist (read before editing)

1. **Obey this file** — Rules below are binding. If a change conflicts with them, align the implementation with these rules (or update the rules **and** `README.md` together after an explicit product decision).
2. **Docs** — **Dual rules files:** from **any** Cursor tab (Chat, Agent, Composer, etc.), whenever you change agent conventions in **either** `.cursor/rules/simple-theme-options.mdc`, update **both** copies in the **same** turn — see the blockquote above. Any user-visible behavior, field API, save shape, responsive semantics, or admin UX change: update **`README.md`** (plugin root) **and** keep this **`.cursor/rules/simple-theme-options.mdc`** **and** its outer twin (`wp-content/plugins/simple-theme-options/.cursor/rules/simple-theme-options.mdc` from a full WordPress install root) in sync when behavior or “how it works” changes. Whenever changes ship, **`README.md`** and the **HTML guide bundle** at **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/`** (relative to this plugin root — same as **`<WordPress-root>/docs/simple-theme-options/`**) must stay aligned. **Mandatory:** whenever you **add or modify** a field type, sample section, hook contract, save/validation behavior, or Theme Settings admin UX, update that bundle in the **same** change set. Keep **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/instructions.html`** current when navigation, field-type inventory, registration examples, or “how to use” workflows change. The guide is aimed at **integrators** (custom `Sections.php` + `Fields/…` modules); keep **core bootstrap** (`Plugin.php`, internal hooks order) in **README** / this **Architecture** section rather than duplicating long internal excerpts in the HTML guide. It is a **three-column** doc (nav | prose | **PHP only**); centre column uses **PHP →** links to the right column; **`html.sto-docs-root`** locks scrolling to the three panes (no extra window scrollbar). **Scroll sync is bidirectional:** scrolling the **centre** updates the **nav** and **PHP** column to the matching sample; scrolling the **PHP** column scrolls the **centre** so the same sample stays aligned and the **nav** follows. PHP snippets ship **Copy** (clipboard) on every block; **Live preview** appears only when **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/sto-instructions-preview-templates.html`** defines **`<template data-sto-preview="{id_suffix}">`** matching **`section id="php-{id_suffix}"`**. To rebuild from a legacy copy that still contains **`<div id="instr-preview-templates">`** and **`<pre data-instr-preview="…">`** blocks in `<main>`, from the WordPress site root run **`node docs/simple-theme-options/rebuild-instructions-layout.mjs`**, or from this plugin folder **`node ../../docs/simple-theme-options/rebuild-instructions-layout.mjs`** (styles + previews: **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/instructions-layout-wc.css`** + **`sto-instructions-preview-templates.html`**; the rebuild embeds the preview templates into the output).
3. **Viewport** — Width → breakpoint tiers live only in **`ViewportOptions::built_in_minimum_widths()`** / **`ViewportOptions::get_minimums()`** (no Theme Settings Advanced UI for thresholds; legacy **`sto_adv_vp_*`** keys are not used for resolution).
4. **Responsive defaults & `device`** — **`ResponsiveConfig::DEFAULT_RESPONSIVE_TABS`** = **`xxl`**, **`md`**, **`mobile`**. Non-empty **`device`** is **union-merged** with that trio in **`ResponsiveConfig::breakpoints_for_field()`** (dedupe, **`ResponsiveConfig::ALL_BREAKPOINTS`** order). Invalid **`device`** slugs are dropped; all invalid ⇒ default trio only.
5. **`required` / eval slice** — **`ResponsiveConfig::REQUIRED_EVAL_BREAKPOINT`** = **`xxl`**. Admin: **`data-sto-require-eval-bp`** on responsive rows; **`getOptionFieldValue( key, '' )`** / **`applyRequiredVisibility`** use that slice, not the active tab. If a field’s tabs omit **`xxl`**, PHP/JS renderers fall back eval to the **first** tab. When reading **one scalar** from a stored breakpoint map in PHP, use **`ResponsiveConfig::value_for_required_eval()`** (or **`raw_value_at_breakpoint()`** where appropriate) — **do not** use **`isset( $map['xxl'] ) ? … : reset( $map )`** (order bugs for **`lg` / `md` / `mobile`-only maps**).
6. **Legacy storage** — **`ResponsiveConfig::raw_value_at_breakpoint()`**: **`phone`** → **`mobile`**; if **`xxl`** is absent but **`lg`** is present, legacy desktop-under-**`lg`** maps still populate the **`xxl`** read path until re-saved.
7. **Responsive tab tooltips** — **`ResponsiveControl`**: native **`title`** = short label (**XXL**, **Tablet**, **Mobile**, … — **`tab_short_title()`**); **`aria-label`** stays fuller (**`aria_labels()`**).
8. **Field UI** — New or changed option rows: **`FieldTitle`** for titles/tooltips; **`required`** contract + **`main.js`** **`getOptionFieldValue`** when storage or DOM shape changes. **Title row:** image **`?`** sits **directly after the title**; optional **`between_html`** (7th arg) adds a **center** column (**responsive Tabs** or **responsive Accordion**: horizontal master strip only — **`$trailing_html`** empty on those composite rows). **Scalar** responsive fields and **each inner field inside responsive Tabs / Accordion** keep device tabs in that row’s **`FieldTitle`** **`$trailing_html`** (right). See **`FieldTitle`** / **`sto-switcher.css`** / **`sto-tabs.css`** / **`sto-accordion.css`**. **Text-like controls** (input, native select, Select2, range number/suffix, typography, color hex + swatch, quick search) use **`--sto-field-soft-*`** custom properties on **`.sto-option-panel-wrapper`** in **`style.css`** (soft border + idle shadow + focus stack) — see **`README.md`** changelog; new fields that render text inputs or select shells should reuse those variables or the same hex fallbacks.
9. **New field types — responsive (mandatory)** — Any **new** Theme Settings field class (or new **shape** of an existing type) **must** implement optional **`responsive`** + **`device`** end-to-end on the same contract as **Select**, **Range**, **Color**, etc.: register **`responsive_breakpoints`** from **`ResponsiveConfig::breakpoints_for_field()`**, render **`data-sto-responsive="1"`**, **`data-sto-active-bp`**, **`data-sto-require-eval-bp`**, and **`ResponsiveControl`** toolbar + panes (typically via **`ResponsiveControl::toolbar_markup()`** in **`FieldTitle::render_heading( …, $trailing_html )`** for standalone rows), per-breakpoint **`name`** + **`sto_options[id][bp]`** (or equivalent for compound ids), save sanitization per slice, **`getOptionFieldValue`** + **`RequiredVisibility`** parity, and **`main.js`** / **`initStoResponsiveTabs`** re-init when the control needs Select2 / pickers / etc. **Do not ship** a new field without this unless you add an **explicit carve-out** (what + why) in **this file** and **`README.md`**. Composite fields (e.g. **Tabs**, **Accordion**) must **inherit** **`responsive` / `device`** onto inner registrations when the parent opts in **and** the inner field does not already define **`responsive`**. **Carve-out — `PARENT_RESPONSIVE_PANE_BP`:** when a field config sets **`ResponsiveConfig::PARENT_RESPONSIVE_PANE_BP`** to a breakpoint slug that exists in **`responsive_breakpoints`**, supported renderers output **one** control for that slice only (class **`sto-field-row--tabs-pane-slice`**, no nested **`data-sto-responsive`** / inner **`ResponsiveControl`** panes) while **save shape** stays **`sto_options[id][bp]`**. **`Tabs`** / **`Accordion`** themselves **do not** set this on inners anymore (each inner owns full breakpoint UI). Adding a new inner field type inside **Tabs** or **Accordion** must respect **`parent_responsive_pane_bp()`** when non-empty. **Tabs / Accordion inner `width` / grid:** each inner field’s **`width`** maps to a **1–12** column span inside **`.sto-tabs__grid`** / **`.sto-accordion__grid`**; keep each **row’s spans summing to ≤12** so the grid does not wrap oddly; **`sto-tabs.css`** must define **`sto-tabs__cell--span-1` … `--span-12`** (omitting **`--span-12`** makes full-width / `1-1` cells default to one column and crushes nested groups). **`sto-tabs.css`** / **`sto-accordion.css`** force one column per inner field at **max-width 960px**; the responsive **master** title row (**title · master strip** only) stacks at **782px**. **Tabs** and **Accordion** **`fields`** trees may include **nested `tabs`**, **`accordion`**, and **subgroups** (`id` + `title` + `fields`, no top-level **`options`**); ids are auto-scoped when nested. **Accordion `panels`:** all sections start **collapsed** unless a panel sets **`expanded`**, **`show`**, or **`open`** (first match wins); **`sto-accordion.js`** collapses when clicking the **active** header or **active** responsive master tab again.
10. **Verify** — Run **`php -l`** on edited PHP files.
11. **Git workflow (commit + push every change)** — Every change to this plugin ends with **`git add` → `git commit` → `git push origin main`** run from the **plugin root** (this folder — the plugin is its own git repo, scoped to itself; from a full WordPress install run the same commands from inside **`wp-content/plugins/simple-theme-options/`**). Remote: **`git@github.com:mdhemalakanda/simple-theme-options.git`** (HTTPS view: **`https://github.com/mdhemalakanda/simple-theme-options`** — **private**). **`gh auth status`** must show **`mdhemalakanda`** before pushing; if another account is active, instruct **`gh auth login -h github.com`** or **`gh auth switch`** once, then continue — see **## Git workflow → Auth** and **Agent authorization**. Imperative commit subjects ≤72 chars (optional body for **why** + user-visible changes). **Never** force-push or rewrite published history on **`main`** (no `--force`, no `--amend` once pushed, no interactive rebase of public commits). **Never** commit secrets, `wp-config.php`, `.htaccess`, `.env*`, `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, build / cache dirs, `*.log`, or zipped builds of the plugin itself — extend **`.gitignore`** (plugin root) instead. **No matter which Cursor surface produced the work** (Chat, Agent, Composer, inline edit, …), the same change set that touches PHP / JS / CSS / docs **must** also produce a clean commit + push before the task is reported complete. See **`## Git workflow`** below for the full ritual.

## Architecture

- Namespace: `SimpleThemeOptions\`; autoload from `includes/` (see `simple-theme-options.php`).
- **Tabs inner clones** carry **`ResponsiveConfig::TABS_INNER_FIELD`** and non-empty **`group`** (`Tabs` **`id`** when standalone) so **`{Input,Select,…}::render_section_fields`** skips them — they render only inside **Tabs** markup (avoids duplicate rows + nested responsive toolbars).
- **Accordion inner clones** carry **`ResponsiveConfig::ACCORDION_INNER_FIELD`** (same skip contract). **`ResponsiveConfig::is_composite_inner_field()`** is the shared guard in field **`render_section_fields`** implementations.
- Admin bootstrap: `Plugin` (for **`manage_options`** users) → **`SampleFieldModules::boot()`** (auto-instantiates **`includes/Admin/Sample/Fields/*/{PascalCase}.php`** singletons, then **`Sections::register()`**) → **`ThemeSettingsAdminBar::instance()`** → **`Sample\Menu::instance()`** → **`Sample\Menu::init()`** only calls **`Options\Menu::register()`** → `include_fields()` fires **`sto_include_option_fields`** (built-in field **`register()`** / **`register_many()`** calls made earlier are queued and flushed at hook priority **`0`** via **`FieldRegistrationDeferral`** — you normally **do not** add your own **`add_action( 'sto_include_option_fields', … )`** just to register fields).
- **Image tooltips:** optional `tooltip` / `tooltip_image` on **Select**, **DynamicObject**, **ImageSelect**, **Color**, **BackgroundControl**, **Typography**, **Switcher**, and **Group** / nested subgroup headings — rendered only via **`Admin\Options\Fields\Common\FieldTitle`**; JS in **`main.js`** (single popover, image cache, optional preloader image/video). See **Field headings & image tooltips** below.
- Section body: hook **`sto_render_section_content`** (`$section_slug`, `$section`, `$menu`). Priorities: standalone **ImageSelect** **17** → standalone **ButtonGroup** **17.5** → standalone **Select** + **DynamicObject** + **Switcher** + **CheckboxControl** **18** (same priority; hook registration order decides print order—boot **`Switcher::instance()`** before **`Select::instance()`** if switchers should appear first; boot **`CheckboxControl::instance()`** alongside **`Switcher`** when you need checkbox rows in a predictable position vs selects; boot **`DynamicObject::instance()`** after **`Select::instance()`** if dynamic CPT rows should follow static selects) → standalone **Color** **19** → standalone **BackgroundControl** **19.25** → standalone **LinkColor** **19.3** → standalone **BorderControl** **19.30** → standalone **ShadowControl** **19.31** → standalone **GradientControl** **19.32** → standalone **Range** **19.35** → standalone **DateField** **19.38** → standalone **DateTimeField** **19.39** → standalone **Dimension** **19.42** → standalone **DividerControl** **19.44** → standalone **Tabs** **19.45** → standalone **Accordion** **19.46** → standalone **CodeEditor** **19.55** → standalone **Input** **19.5** → standalone **Typography** **20** → **Group** **21** → sample section chrome (e.g. save row) **30**.
- **Admin bar:** `ThemeSettingsAdminBar` enqueues **`dashicons`** + **`sto-admin-bar-theme-settings`** and maps each section’s **`icon`** / slug to a **`dashicons-*`** class (filter **`sto_admin_bar_dashicon`**) — FA webfonts are **not** bundled, so the toolbar does **not** use `<i class="fa-…">`. **`sto-admin-bar-theme-settings.css`** keeps the first `.ab-submenu` as a **vertical block** and fixes nested flyout **`margin-top`**. `Plugin` loads `Sample\Menu` only when **`current_user_can( 'manage_options' )`**. Extend with **`sto_admin_bar_theme_settings_registered`**. Use **`Options\Menu::get_theme_settings_url( $slug )`** for deep links.
- **Theme Settings page nav:** `Menu::get_section_markup()` uses **`sto-option-panel-nav-layout`** (flex: left rail + main). Top-level items with children render a **nested vertical** **`ul.sto-option-panel-sidebar-children`** under the parent row (`ul > li > ul`), toggled with **`sto-is-open` / `sto-is-collapsed`** (chevrons **`fa-angle-up` / `fa-angle-down`**). Server-side **`sto-is-parent-active`** when the current leaf is under that parent. Parent row **`href`** targets the **first leaf** section; **`get_theme_settings_url()`** resolves any parent slug to a leaf; **`redirect_theme_settings_to_canonical_leaf()`** + **`submenu_file`** keep the URL and WP left submenu highlight aligned with that leaf’s top-level group. Each sidebar **`li`** has **`data-sto-section`** (own slug); **`main.js`** `syncActiveState` resolves **parent** URL slugs to a leaf via **`resolveSectionToLeafSlug()`**, matches **`data-sto-section ===` leaf**, **`replaceState`** canonicalizes the URL, and **`simple_theme_options.sto_nav.wp_submenu_for_leaf`** aligns **`#adminmenu .current`** with registered submenu slugs. Sections registered with **`add_section( $name, $slug, $icon, array( 'nav_locked' => true ) )`** are sorted **last** in the sidebar, WP submenu, admin bar section list, quick-search section index, and **leaf form panels** (`get_sections_for_navigation()`, `get_leaf_sections_for_navigation()`); locked rows get **`sto-option-panel-sidebar-item--nav-locked`** + a screen-reader “Plugin section” hint. **Desktop (≥783px) sticky rail:** **`style.css`** sets **`.sto-option-panel-sidebar-wrap`** to **`position: sticky`**, **`top: calc(var(--wp-admin--admin-bar--height, 32px) + 16px)`** (clears the fixed WP admin bar with breathing room), **`align-self: flex-start`**, **`max-height: calc(100vh - var(--wp-admin--admin-bar--height, 32px) - 24px)`**, and **`overflow-y: auto`** so a long section list scrolls inside the dark panel while the main column scrolls independently. **Narrow admin / touch:** **`style.css`** keeps **`min-width: 0`** on the flex shell, **`.sto-option-panel-wrapper`** (**`width: 100%`**, **`max-width: min(1350px, 100%)`**), field rows, group inners, and section body; **`@media (max-width: 782px)`** stacks sidebar above content (sticky rail rules do not apply), full-widths the header quick search, tightens paddings, resets sticky save bar side margins, and forces **`.sto-option-panel-wrapper .sto-row > *`** to a single column; companion tweaks live in **`sto-input.css`**, **`sto-responsive.css`**, **`sto-range.css`**, and **`sto-switcher.css`** (see **`README.md`** changelog).
- **Viewport (built-in tiers):** Viewport width → breakpoint uses fixed min-width floors in **`ViewportOptions`** (no Theme Settings UI). **`sto_get_responsive_option()`** / **`sto-viewport.js`** use the same cascade. Optional front script **`sto-viewport.js`** — enable with filter **`sto_enqueue_viewport_script`** (see `Assets::enqueue_public_scripts()`).

## Field headings & image tooltips (mandatory for every option UI)

- **Single code path:** Every label row that should show the WoodMart-style **?** image preview must use **`FieldTitle::get_tooltip_config( $config )`** and **`FieldTitle::render_heading( … )`**. Do **not** output **`.sto-field-help-trigger`**, **`.sto-field-title-row`**, **`.sto-field-group-item-title-row`**, or **`.sto-field-group-heading-row`** by hand except inside **`FieldTitle`** itself.
- **Title row layout (fixed product rule):** **`render_heading()`** wraps the heading + **`?`** in **`.sto-field-title-row__leading`** so the help control appears **immediately after the title text**. Optional **`$between_html`** (7th parameter) renders **`.sto-field-title-row__center`** when non-empty (grid row with modifier **`.sto-field-title-row--tabs-master`** — **responsive Tabs** and **responsive Accordion** use it for the horizontal master strip only; inner fields supply their own **`$trailing_html`** device toolbars). **Scalar** responsive fields: breakpoint tabs in **`$trailing_html`** → **`.sto-field-title-row__trailing`**. Do not place **`?`** in the trailing cluster without updating this rule, **`README.md`**, and **`sto-switcher.css`** / **`sto-tabs.css`** / **`sto-accordion.css`** / **`style.css`**.
- **`$context` values:**
  - **`default`** — standalone fields and the main title inside **`.sto-field-row`**: **`<h4>`** + **`.sto-field-title-sep`** under the label.
  - **`group_inner`** — fields rendered inside **`.sto-field-group-inner`**: **`<h5>`** + optional inner sep; for **`image_select`** pass **`$inner_include_sep = true`** so the rule prints like other inner fields.
  - **`group_panel`** — **Group** / nested subgroup panel title: **`<h3 class="sto-field-group-heading">`** inside **`.sto-field-group-heading-row`** (no title-sep; description follows as today).
- **Config shape** (field register array, **`Group::register()`** root config, or nested subgroup item): **`tooltip` => array( 'image' => URL, 'preloader' => optional URL )** **or** legacy **`tooltip_image`** + optional **`tooltip_preloader`**. The **?** button appears only when **`get_tooltip_config`** resolves a non-empty **`image`** URL.
- **New field types:** When you add a new options field class, its **`render_field_markup()`** (or equivalent) **must** call **`FieldTitle`** for the human-readable **title** the same way **Select**, **Switcher**, **Color**, **BackgroundControl**, **Typography**, **Range**, **Dimension**, **DividerControl**, **Tabs** (via **`FieldTitle`** on the tab strip row), **Accordion** (via **`FieldTitle`** on the composite row), **ImageSelect**, **DynamicObject**, and **Input** do. Skipping this is considered an incomplete implementation. It **must** also implement the **responsive** contract (checklist §9): **`responsive` / `device`**, toolbar + panes, per-breakpoint storage, save + JS + **`required`** parity — same bar as existing scalar fields; composite types propagate to children.

## Where to register sample fields (by admin section)

- Put option registrations in **`includes/Admin/Sample/Fields/{Section}/{Section}.php`** (PascalCase folder + class; e.g. **`Fields/General/General.php`** registers **`section_slug`** leaves such as **`layout-nav`**, **`layout-type`**, … under parent **`field-samples`**; **`Fields/Appearance/Appearance.php`** for **`appearance-color`** / **`appearance-gradient`** / **`appearance-surfaces`** / **`appearance-links`**; **`Fields/Accordion/AccordionDemo.php`** for the single **`accordion`** leaf with every accordion demo). **`Sample\Sections.php`** defines parent sections + subsection leaves where used (nested sidebar + admin bar flyouts).
- Namespace: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Sample\Fields\{Section}\{ClassName}`** (e.g. **`…\Accordion\AccordionDemo`**).
- Boot sample field modules via **`SampleFieldModules::boot()`** from **`Plugin::register_hooks()`** (before **`Sample\Menu::instance()`**). It scans **`Fields/*/{PascalCase}.php`**, requires matching FQCN + **`instance()`**, calls **`{Class}::instance()`**, then **`Sections::instance()->register()`** — add a new folder + class file only; **`Sample\Menu::init()`** stays menu-only.
- One class per file: `init()` calls **`Foo::register()`** / **`Foo::register_many()`** (and boots other field singletons first when you care about **`sto_render_section_content`** hook order among types at the same priority — see §Architecture above); registrations apply on **`sto_include_option_fields`** automatically. **Registry reads without `::instance()`:** field classes compose **`FieldSingletonAccessors`** — use **`Foo::get_field( $section, $id )`**, **`Foo::get_field_ids_for_section( $section )`**, **`Foo::is_registered_field_id( $id )`**, **`Foo::get_all_fields_for_search()`**, and (where implemented) **`Foo::sanitize_posted_value( $id, $raw )`** instead of **`Foo::instance()->…`** (the instance implementations are named **`registry_*`** so they never collide with those **`public static`** façades — see **`README.md` Fix notes**). **Theme CSS value helpers** on **`BorderControl`** / **`ShadowControl`** / **`GradientControl`** (`value_to_css_border`, `value_to_css_box_shadow`, `get_css_rule_string`, `get_value_array`, `value_to_css_background_image`) are **instance-only** — PHP forbids a same-named **`static`** alias; use **`::instance()->…`** or **`sto_get_shadow_*()`** / **`sto_get_gradient_background_image()`** (see **`README.md` Fix notes**). **Every built-in field type (`Group`, `Tabs`, `Accordion`, `Switcher`, `CheckboxControl`, `Color`, `BorderControl`, `ShadowControl`, `GradientControl`, `CodeEditor`, `Input`, `Select`, `ImageSelect`, `ButtonGroup`, `Range`, `Typography`, `Dimension`, `BackgroundControl`, `DynamicObject`, `LinkColor`) exposes `register()` and `register_many()` as `public static` methods** (added 2026-05) — they internally call `static::instance()` and pass the registration through **`FieldRegistrationDeferral::defer_or_run()`**, so the boot ordering / hook priority rules are unchanged. New field types must add the same **static** `register()` / `register_many()` entry-points; keep the actual registration logic in an instance-level helper (e.g. `register_field_config()`) invoked via the captured `$instance` inside the deferred closure. Use **`Foo::instance()`** (no `->register(…)`) when you only need to boot the singleton early for hook-order purposes.
- Boot field APIs you use in that file’s **`init()`** (e.g. **`ImageSelect::instance()`**, **`Select::instance()`**, **`DynamicObject::instance()`**, **`Input::instance()`**, **`DateField::instance()`**, **`DateTimeField::instance()`**, **`Dimension::instance()`**, **`DividerControl::instance()`**, **`Range::instance()`**, **`Tabs::instance()`**, **`Accordion::instance()`**, **`Switcher::instance()`**, **`CheckboxControl::instance()`**, **`Group::instance()`**, **`Color::instance()`**, **`GradientControl::instance()`**, **`BackgroundControl::instance()`**, **`Typography::instance()`**) **before** the first **`register()`** that needs their render hooks to attach in a specific order — singletons are safe to call from multiple section files.

## Select fields

- Use **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\Select\Select`** → `register()` / `register_many()`.
- Required config: `section_slug`, `id`, `options` (map value → label). Optional: `title`, `description`, `default`, `placeholder`, `class`, `wrapper_class`, **`required`**, **`multiple`** (bool), **`max`** (int when **`multiple`**, **0** = unlimited; capped at **100**), **`tooltip`**, **`responsive`**, **`device`**.
- **Multi-select (`multiple` => true):** stored value is **`array<int, string>`** (option keys) in **`sto_options[id]`** — or **`array<bp, array<int, string>>`** when **`responsive`**. **`default`** accepts an array or comma list; unknown keys are dropped. POST omits the key when zero chips remain — **`Select::merge_missing_multiple_select_fields()`** persists cleared selections as **`[]`** per breakpoint or top-level for that section only (called from **`Menu::maybe_handle_save_request()`** before **`CheckboxControl::merge_missing_multiple_checkbox_fields()`** and **`DynamicObject::merge_missing_multiple_dynamic_fields()`**). Renders as **`<select multiple>`** with **`name="sto_options[id][]"`** (or **`sto_options[id][bp][]`** for responsive); each saved key gets a `<option selected>`. The `<select>` carries **`data-multiple="1"`**, **`data-max-selections="<n>"`**, **`data-placeholder-text="..."`** — **`main.js`** **`initStoSelect2`** reads these to enable **`multiple: true`** + **`maximumSelectionLength`** + multi placeholder (no **`allowClear`** for multi). Chips are styled in **`sto-select2.css`** under **`.select2-selection--multiple`** / **`.select2-selection__choice`** — blue (**#2271b1**) background with white text and a leading white "×" remove icon. **`required`** matching against a multi-select compares the **comma-joined** ordered list (same as **`<select multiple>`** **`.val()`**), so a single expected value matches only when it is the **only** picked chip; server-side parity via **`RequiredVisibility::value_as_string`**.
- Do **not** set `group` manually; **`Group`** sets it for inner fields.
- Standalone fields: **image_select** (**17**) → **select** + **dynamic_object** + **switcher** + **checkbox** (**18**) → **color** (**19**) → **background_control** (**19.25**) → **link_color** (**19.3**) → **border** (**19.30**) → **shadow** (**19.31**) → **gradient** (**19.32**) → **range** (**19.35**) → **date** (**19.38**) → **datetime** (**19.39**) → **dimension** (**19.42**) → **tabs** (**19.45**) → **accordion** (**19.46**) → **code_editor** (**19.55**) → **input** (**19.5**) → **typography** (**20**) → **groups** (**21**). Within each type, order matches `register()` / `register_many()` order. Fields with non-empty **`group`** are **not** rendered in the standalone passes; they render inside their group in `fields` order.

## Dynamic Object (CPT select)

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\DynamicObject\DynamicObject`** → `register()` / `register_many()`.
- Required: `section_slug`, `id`, **`post_type`**. Optional: **`multiple`** (bool), **`max`** (max selections when multiple, **0** = unlimited), **`limit`** (AJAX page size, default **10** — not preloaded in HTML), **`search_min_length`** (default **3**; AJAX + Select2), `title`, `description`, `default` (post ID string, or array / comma list when **`multiple`**), `placeholder`, **`post_status`**, `class`, `wrapper_class`, **`required`**, **`tooltip`**, **`responsive`** (same semantics as **Select** / **Color**).
- Stored value: **post ID** string or empty (single), or **array of post ID strings** (multiple); per-breakpoint maps when **`responsive`**; save: **`DynamicObject::sanitize_for_field()`** via **`Menu::maybe_handle_save_request()`**; **`merge_missing_multiple_dynamic_fields( $posted, $sanitized, $section_key_map )`** (optional third map = current leaf’s field ids) persists cleared multi-select as **`[]`** per breakpoint or top-level for that section only.
- **Inside a group:** **`'type' => 'dynamic_object'`** plus the same keys (omit `section_slug`).
- AJAX: **`wp_ajax_sto_dynamic_object_search`** — returns up to **`limit`** matches per page only when the search string length is ≥ **`search_min_length`**; shorter queries return empty `results`. Localized as **`simple_theme_options.sto_dynamic_object`** (includes **`i18n.input_too_short`** for Select2). Query args filter: **`sto_dynamic_object_query_args`**. Post-type gate filter: **`sto_dynamic_object_is_post_type_allowed`**.

## Select2 (admin)

- Bundled under `assets/admin/vendor/select2/`. Enqueued only on Theme Settings (`page=theme-settings`) via `Assets`.
- Selects use class **`sto-input-select`**. **Dynamic Object** adds **`sto-dynamic-object`**; **`initStoSelect2`** in **`main.js`** initializes plain selects and dynamic CPT selects (AJAX, **`minimumInputLength`** from **`data-search-min`**, default **3**) separately. Init/re-init: `refreshStoSelect2()` after section switch and after **`change`** on `.sto-options-form` (also **`stoInitColorPickers`**, **`stoInitTypographyPanels`**, **`stoInitBackgroundControls`**, **`stoInitBorderControls`**, **`stoInitShadowControls`**, **`stoInitGradientControls`**, **`stoInitRangeControls`**, **`stoInitDateFields`**, **`stoInitDateTimeFields`**, **`stoInitDimensionFields`**, **`stoInitCheckboxControls`**, **`stoInitTabsControls`**, **`stoInitAccordionControls`**).

## Conditional visibility — `required`

### New field types — `required` compatibility (mandatory)

Whenever you **add or change a field type**, treat **`required` / conditional visibility as a first-class requirement**. The full chain must work: **this field** respects **`required`**, **other fields** that depend on **this field’s** value update correctly, and **this field** updates when **its** dependencies change.

**Checklist (all must pass before the field type is done):**

1. **Wrapper** — Outer shell is **`.sto-field-row`** or **`.sto-field-group`** (or nested group), with **`data-sto-required`** when the field or group uses **`required`** (same JSON schema as existing fields).
2. **DOM value for rules** — The stored value must be readable for condition matching. Prefer **`name="sto_options[{id}]"`** (single) or **`name="sto_options[{id}][{breakpoint}]"`** / **`sto_options[{id}][{breakpoint}][]`** when responsive. Update **`main.js`** **`getOptionFieldValue( fieldKey, contextBp )`** so it returns the **exact** value **`required`** compares to (radios → **`:checked`**, checkboxes, multi-select → joined ids, hidden sync inputs, JSON fields, etc.).
3. **Hidden = inert** — Hidden rows use **`sto-required-hidden`**; **`applyRequiredVisibility`** disables **`:input`** inside the wrapper. All submit inputs for that option must live **inside** that wrapper.
4. **Events** — User changes must fire **`change`** on **`.sto-options-form :input`** (or call **`window.stoApplyDependentFieldVisibility`**). **Select2:** **`main.js`** also listens for **`select2:select` / `select2:clear` / `select2:unselect`** on Theme Settings selects so **`required`** updates after AJAX picks. Revealed fields that need **Select2** / color init must be covered by **`refreshStoSelect2()`** (and existing re-init hooks).
5. **Groups** — **`markEmptyFieldGroups`** expects **`.sto-field-row`** / nested **`.sto-field-group`** under **`.sto-field-group-inner`**; do not break that structure.
6. **Manual test** — Verify: (a) this field hides/shows per its **`required`**; (b) dependents of **this** field toggle both ways; (c) save + reload still behaves.

If the type introduces a **new** storage or naming pattern, **update `getOptionFieldValue`** and document it in this file and **`README.md`**. Do not ship a field type that breaks **`required`** for itself or dependents.

---

- Output: `data-sto-required` JSON on the **wrapper** (`.sto-field-row` or `.sto-field-group`).
- JS: `assets/admin/js/main.js` — `applyRequiredVisibility()` (multi-pass until **`sto-required-hidden`** stabilizes); hidden rows get **`sto-required-hidden`**; inputs inside disabled when hidden. **`findOptionInputsByName()`** prefers the active **`.sto-option-panel-section.sto-is-active`**, then **`.sto-options-form`**, when resolving **`name`** for **`getOptionFieldValue`**.
- **`getOptionFieldValue( fieldKey )` must stay accurate for every input shape** used in Theme Settings:
  - **Radio groups** share `name="sto_options[field]"` — always read **`:checked`** (never `.first()` only).
  - **Checkboxes:** single = checked + value; multiple same name = join checked values (comma-separated) if you use that pattern.
  - Otherwise **select / hidden / text** = first matching name or `#id` fallback; **responsive** rows use **`sto_options[fieldKey][breakpoint]`** (and **`sto_options[fieldKey][breakpoint][]`** for **DynamicObject** multiple). For **`required`** matching, **`applyRequiredVisibility`** always reads the **eval / PC** breakpoint (**`data-sto-require-eval-bp`** on the dependency row, default **`xxl`**), not the active device tab. **Typography** / **Background control** / **Range**: per-pane or single hidden JSON under the same naming; **non-responsive** = one hidden **`sto_options[fieldKey]`**. **Tabs** / **Accordion** (standalone or inside **Group**): each inner control still uses flat **`sto_options[{composite_id}]`** when non-responsive, or the same **per-breakpoint map** on that composite key when the parent row has **`responsive`** — **`getOptionFieldValue`** uses the same **`fieldKey`** as the registered composite id. **Classic `wp_editor`**: when TinyMCE visual mode is active, read content via **`tinymce.get(id)`** (see **`readInputValue`** in **`main.js`**).
- Changing or adding field types: update **`getOptionFieldValue`** if the control does not use a single named input with a simple `.val()`.
- **Direct** (single AND group):

```php
'required' => array(
	'layout_header' => 'none',
),
```

- **Nested** (OR of AND groups):

```php
'required' => array(
	array( 'layout_header' => 'none' ),
	array( 'other_field' => 'value' ),
),
```

- Semantics: conditions inside one object = **AND**; multiple arrays = **OR**. Same schema for **per-field** and **whole-group** `required` on `Group::register()`.
- After `applyRequiredVisibility`, **`markEmptyFieldGroups`** adds **`sto-field-group--empty-body`** when a group’s inner has no visible `.sto-field-row` / nested groups (avoids empty nested shells when children are all `sto-required-hidden`).

## Responsive breakpoints (`responsive` + optional `device`)

- **Canonical keys** (full palette): **`xxl`**, **`xl`**, **`lg`**, **`md`**, **`sm`**, **`xs`**, **`mobile`**. Register with **`'responsive' => true`** or **`'responsive' => array( … )`** (non-empty array only **opts in**; the array contents are not used as the device list — use **`device`** for that).
- **Default tabs** when **`device`** is omitted or empty: **`xxl`** (desktop / PC), **`md`** (tablet), **`mobile`** — see **`ResponsiveConfig::DEFAULT_RESPONSIVE_TABS`**. Viewport → key uses built-in floors in **`ViewportOptions`** (not user-editable). **Legacy:** stored maps with desktop under **`lg`** (old trio) still resolve into the **`xxl`** slice on read via **`ResponsiveConfig::raw_value_at_breakpoint()`** until re-saved.
- **Optional subset / merge:** **`'device' => array( 'lg', 'xl', … )`** — each slug is **merged** with **`ResponsiveConfig::DEFAULT_RESPONSIVE_TABS`** (union, UI order **xxl → mobile**). Overlapping keys (e.g. **`md`** in both) appear once. Invalid slugs are dropped; **`phone`** maps to **`mobile`**. If every slug in **`device`** is invalid, only the **default trio** is used.
- **Legacy:** Saved maps may use **`phone`** instead of **`mobile`**; **`ResponsiveConfig`** reads **`phone`** into **`mobile`**; new saves write **`mobile`** only.
- **PHP:** **`Admin\Options\Fields\Common\ResponsiveConfig`** (`breakpoints_for_field` merges **`device`** with **`DEFAULT_RESPONSIVE_TABS`**, `ordered_device_subset`), **`ResponsiveControl`** (title-row icon tabs + panes; each tab has a short **`title`** on hover, e.g. **XXL** / **Tablet**). Row: **`data-sto-responsive="1"`**, **`data-sto-active-bp`** (which pane is visible — not used for **`required`**), **`data-sto-require-eval-bp`** on each responsive row (slice used for **`required`** + server **`value_for_required_eval`** — default **`xxl`**). **`RequiredVisibility`** / admin **`getOptionFieldValue( key, '' )`** evaluate **`required`** at the eval slice only.
- **Implemented field types:** **Switcher**, **Select**, **ButtonGroup**, **ImageSelect**, **Color**, **Input** (not **`editor`**), **Typography**, **BackgroundControl**, **LinkColor**, **DynamicObject**, **Range**, **Tabs**, **Accordion** (responsive on the parent row propagates to inner composites). Each registers **`responsive_breakpoints`**, renders panes + **`sto_options[id][bp]`** (or **`sto_options[id][bp][]`** for DynamicObject multiple), and uses **`sanitize_posted_value`** / **`sanitize_for_field`** on save via **`Menu::maybe_handle_save_request()`**.
- **New field types:** **Must** follow the same responsive contract (not optional): **`ResponsiveConfig::breakpoints_for_field()`**, toolbar + panes (typically **`FieldTitle`** **`$trailing_html`**), per-BP **`name`**, **`main.js`** **`getOptionFieldValue`** (including **`[]`** names for multi-select), **`initStoResponsiveTabs`** re-init (Select2, color pickers, typography, background, range, **each responsive field inside Tabs / Accordion grids**, …), server **`RequiredVisibility`** parity, and **`README.md`** + this file. See **Mandatory agent checklist** §9.

## Typography field

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\Typography\Typography`**. Register standalone or in **`Group`** with **`type` => `typography`**. Value = JSON per breakpoint or single JSON in **`sto_options[id]`** (`family`, `variant`, `subset`, `transform`); save via **`Typography::sanitize_posted_value()`** in **`Menu`** (delegates to **`sanitize_stored_value()`** per slice).
- Catalog: **`Data\TypographyFontsCatalog`**, AJAX **`sto_typography_fonts`**, filter **`sto_typography_font_catalog`**. UI: **`sto-typography.js`** / **`sto-typography.css`** — no tinted panel (flush in group), **2×2 grid**, Select2 clear+chevron like **`sto-select2.css`**, **one-line preview** + scroll, weights filtered by family.

## Color field

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\Color\Color`**. Register standalone or in **`Group`** with **`type` => `color`**. Value = **`#rrggbb`** or **`rgb`/`rgba`** in **`sto_options[id]`**; save via **`Color::sanitize_stored_value()`** in **`Menu`**.
- Default **`alpha` => true** (transparency): requires **`data-alpha-enabled="true"`** + **`data-type="full"`** on the input and vendor **`wp-color-picker-alpha`** (`assets/admin/vendor/wp-color-picker-alpha/`, GPLv2+). Set **`alpha` => false** for hex-only.
- Optional **`palettes`**: Iris preset row; **`sto-color.js`** reads **`data-sto-palettes`**. Standalone **`.sto-field-row-color`** and embedded pickers under **`.sto-field-row-gradient`** share the same **`wp-color-picker`** chrome — **`sto-color.css`** uses **`:is(.sto-field-row-color, .sto-field-row-gradient)`** so Iris holder, **`palette_ui`** grids, and swatch sizing match. Rows render flush like other regular fields. UI: **`wp-color-picker`** + **`sto-color.css`** / **`sto-color.js`**; **`refreshStoSelect2`** → **`stoInitColorPickers`**; **`change`/`clear`** + reset → **`stoApplyDependentFieldVisibility`**.
- Optional **`palette_ui`**: preset chrome variant — **`classic`** (default, single-row Iris swatches), **`advanced`** (wrapping **CSS grid** of rounded tiles, softer popover shell, overrides Iris %/float swatch layout), **`advanced-circles`** (larger circular swatches), **`advanced-dense`** (compact grid for many presets). When **`palette_ui`** is not **`classic`** and **`palettes`** is empty, **`Color`** injects a built-in extended list (filter **`sto_color_built_in_advanced_palettes`**). Markup adds **`data-sto-palette-ui`** and **`sto-color-wrap--palette-*`** on **`.sto-color-wrap`**; **`sto-color.css`** grids **`.iris-palette-container`** and styles **`a.iris-palette`** (Iris: swatches are anchors **inside** the container — do **not** grid **`.iris-picker .iris-palette`** alone, it matches each swatch and caused full-width bars). **Layout:** Iris defaults **`position:absolute; bottom:0`** on **`.iris-palette-container`** (strip over the SV square); advanced UI uses **`position:relative`**, **`clear:both`**, **`height:auto`** on **`.iris-picker`**, fluid **`repeat(auto-fit, minmax(…, 1fr))`** tracks, wider **`.wp-picker-holder`** (cap ~**520px**); **`sto-color.js`** **`reflowPaletteUiIrisLayout`** on open clears Iris inline **`height`/`paddingBottom`** and sets each **`.iris-strip`** height to the square so hue/alpha rails match the main panel. **`sto-color.js`** uses **`.iris-palette-container a.iris-palette`** for active swatch sync; **hover / `:focus-within`**, larger Iris handles, responsive tweaks; **`prefers-reduced-motion`** fallbacks.

## Link color field (paired Regular + Hover)

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\LinkColor\LinkColor`**. Register standalone or in **`Group`** with **`type` => `link_color`**. Standalone hook priority **`19.3`** (between **BackgroundControl** **`19.25`** and **Range** **`19.35`**). Value = **JSON** per breakpoint or single JSON: **`{ "regular": "#rrggbb|rgb|rgba", "hover": "#rrggbb|rgb|rgba" }`**; save via **`LinkColor::sanitize_posted_value()`** in **`Menu`** (delegates to **`Color::sanitize_stored_value()`** per sub-color).
- Keys: **`section_slug`**, **`id`**, **`title`**, optional **`description`**, **`default` => array( 'regular' => '#…', 'hover' => '#…' )`** (built-in fallbacks **`#333333`** / **`#222222`**), **`labels` => array( 'regular' => …, 'hover' => …)`** (defaults **Regular** / **Hover**), **`palettes`**, **`alpha`** (default **`true`**, same semantics as **Color**), **`required`**, **`tooltip`**, **`responsive`**, **`device`**, **`class`**, **`wrapper_class`**.
- Markup uses **`.sto-field-row-color`** + **`.sto-field-row-link-color`** so **`sto-color.css`** applies; each sub-state wraps the visible **`wp-color-picker`** input in a **`.sto-color-wrap`** with **`.sto-link-color__input`** (**`data-sto-link-color-key`** = **`regular`** or **`hover`**). One **`<input type="hidden" class="sto-link-color-value" name="sto_options[id]">`** (or **`sto_options[id][bp]`**) submits the merged JSON.
- UI: each picker renders the **full Color-field chrome** — swatch + visible hex / rgba text input (admins can type / paste custom values) + Default / Clear + external **`.sto-color-reset`**; Iris popover with optional alpha + palette opens on swatch click. **`sto-link-color.css`** only lays out two columns side-by-side (label above each picker, text input width ~11em desktop, full width on ≤782px) and otherwise inherits every rule from **`sto-color.css`** (soft border / focus tokens, alpha checkerboard, etc.). **Do not** re-hide **`.wp-picker-input-wrap`** unless you also remove the requirement to type a custom value — admins rely on the text input for paste / manual entry.
- JS: **`sto-link-color.js`** (handle **`sto-link-color`**, deps **`jquery`**, **`sto-color`**, **`display-section-on-menu`**). Listens on each **`.sto-link-color__input`** **`change` / `input`** to re-write the hidden JSON; reset button defers sync to **`setTimeout(0)`** so Iris flushes first (same ordering as **`sto-color.js`**). On **`#sto-theme-settings-options-form` `submit`**, every **`[data-sto-link-color]`** is force-synced. **`stoInitLinkColors`** is invoked from **`refreshStoSelect2()`** and **`initStoResponsiveTabs`** alongside **`stoInitColorPickers`** / **`stoInitBackgroundControls`**.
- **`required` / `getOptionFieldValue`:** the hidden JSON uses the same **`sto_options[id]`** or **`sto_options[id][bp]`** name as other scalar/JSON fields, so **`getOptionFieldValue`** reads it directly (string compare against the full JSON payload). For conditional rules that need to inspect one sub-color, compare the saved JSON string or wire a custom helper.
- **Carve-out — Tabs inner type:** **LinkColor is not (yet) registrable as an inner field inside `Tabs`** (`type` => `tabs`). The compound composition is not needed for the initial Appearance use case and would require a new inner-type branch in **`Tabs::register_inner_clone()`**. Standalone + **Group** inner are fully wired (responsive + device + Iris + reset + save). Add the Tabs branch + this carve-out removal in the same change if the need arises.
- Sample: **Links color** in **`Sample/Fields/Appearance/Appearance.php`** — Regular **`#333333`** / Hover **`#222222`**, small Iris palette, image tooltip on the title.

## Background control field

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\BackgroundControl\BackgroundControl`**. Register standalone or in **`Group`** with **`type` => `background_control`**. Value = **JSON** per breakpoint or single JSON: **`{ "color": "#rrggbb|rgb|rgba", "image_id": "" | "123" }`**; save via **`BackgroundControl::sanitize_posted_value()`** in **`Menu`**.
- **`default`**: **`array( 'color' => '…', 'image_id' => '' | positive int )`**. Optional **`palettes`**, **`alpha`** (same defaults as **Color**), **`tooltip`**, **`required`**. Row uses **`.sto-field-row-color`** so **`sto-color.css`** applies to the embedded **`wp-color-picker`**; upload uses **`sto-background-control.css`** / **`sto-background-control.js`** (**`wp.media`** — **`Assets`** calls **`wp_enqueue_media()`** on Theme Settings).
- **`refreshStoSelect2`** runs **`stoInitColorPickers`** then **`stoInitBackgroundControls`**. **`getOptionFieldValue`** reads the hidden JSON: **`sto_options[field][breakpoint]`** when the row is responsive, else **`sto_options[field]`** (same pattern as **Typography**).
- **Save path:** **`sto-color.js`** triggers **`change`** on the color input from **`wpColorPicker`** **`change`** / **`clear`** (deferred with **`setTimeout(0)`**) only — **no** synchronous **`stoApplyDependentFieldVisibility`** in that path, so background hidden JSON is synced before **`getOptionFieldValue`** runs. **`main.js`** debounces **`refreshStoSelect2()`** on **`.sto-options-form :input` `change`** (~**180ms**). **`sto-background-control.js`** syncs every control on **`#sto-theme-settings-options-form` `submit`**.

## Border field

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\BorderControl\BorderControl`**. Register standalone or in **`Group`** with **`type` => `border`**. Value = single **JSON** (or per-breakpoint map of JSON) **`{ "radius", "radius_unit", "style", "width", "width_unit", "color" }`** in **`sto_options[id]`** (or **`sto_options[id][bp]`**). Save via **`BorderControl::sanitize_posted_value()`** in **`Menu`**.
- **Register keys:** **`section_slug`**, **`id`**, **`title`**, optional **`description`**, **`default`** (array of the JSON shape; missing keys fill with **`radius: '0'`** / **`radius_unit: 'px'`** / **`style: 'none'`** / **`width: '1'`** / **`width_unit: 'px'`** / **`color: '#000000'`**), optional **`features`** => ordered subset of **`radius`**, **`style`**, **`width`**, **`color`** (default = all four; pass fewer to hide popover rows), optional **`min_radius`** / **`max_radius`** (default **0 – 100**), **`min_width`** / **`max_width`** (default **0 – 20**), **`radius_units`** => subset of **`px` / `%` / `em` / `rem`** (default **`array( 'px' )`** = locked uppercase chip; ≥2 entries renders a small **PX / %** toggle pill group), **`width_units`** => subset of **`px` / `em` / `rem`** (default **`array( 'px' )`**), **`alpha`** (bool, default **true**), **`palettes`**, **`required`**, **`tooltip`**, **`wrapper_class`**, **`responsive`**, **`device`**. Allowed **`style`** values: **`none` / `solid` / `dashed` / `dotted` / `double` / `groove` / `ridge` / `inset` / `outset`**.
- **UI contract:** title row + tiny **↻ row-level reset** chip (rendered inside **`.sto-field-title-row__leading`** after the optional **`?`** help control via **`BorderControl::inject_reset_into_leading()`**) + blue WoodMart-style **"Edit settings"** pill that toggles a **`.sto-border-popover`** floating panel below it. Popover rows render only the enabled **`features`** in order: **Border radius** (slider + number + unit chip / toggle), **Border style** (native styled **`<select>`** — **not** Select2, so a hidden popover can't break sizing), **Border width** (slider + number + unit), **Border color** (full **`wp-color-picker` + alpha** chrome with palette + reset). Outside clicks **except** **`.wp-picker-container`** / **`.iris-picker`** / **`.wp-color-result`** close the popover; **Escape** also closes. **Inside Accordion:** **`.sto-accordion__item`** uses **`overflow: hidden`** for rounded cards — **`sto-accordion.css`** uses **`:has(.sto-border-control[data-sto-border-open="1"])`** → **`overflow: visible`** (+ stacking **`z-index`**) while the popover is open so rows are not clipped.
- **Save / sanitize:** **`BorderControl::sanitize_posted_value()`** clamps each number into **`[min, max]`**, validates the style enum, normalizes units against the registered allow-list, and re-sanitizes color via **`Color::sanitize_stored_value()`** (so any **`#rgb` / `#rrggbb` / `#rrggbbaa` / `rgb()` / `rgba()`** payload is accepted). Helper (instance): **`BorderControl::instance()->value_to_css_border( $field_id )`** returns a `width style color` shorthand (or **`none`**) for theme output; **`BorderControl::instance()->get_value_array( $field_id )`** returns the merged sub-value array using the eval / `xxl` slice when stored as a breakpoint map.
- **Conditional `required`:** **`getOptionFieldValue`** reads the **full JSON string** from the hidden **`.sto-border-value`** input — match the whole string or depend on a sibling scalar field instead of parsing JSON in simple equality rules (same constraint as **BackgroundControl** / **Typography** / **LinkColor**).
- **Hook priority `19.30`** — between **BackgroundControl** (**`19.25`**) and **Range** (**`19.35`**). **`Menu::maybe_handle_save_request()`** registers the field id via **`BorderControl::get_field_ids_for_section()`** in the section key registry; global search index pulls in **`BorderControl::get_all_fields_for_search()`**.
