## Code editor field

- Class: **`SimpleThemeOptions\Admin\Options\Fields\CodeEditor\CodeEditor`**. Register standalone or in **`Group`** with **`type` => `code_editor`** (also accepts the aliases **`codeeditor`** / **`code`**). Value = raw string in **`sto_options[id]`** (or per-breakpoint map **`sto_options[id][xxl|md|mobile]`** when **`responsive`** is set). Save via **`CodeEditor::sanitize_posted_value()`** in **`Menu`**.
- **Runtime:** **`wp.codeEditor`** — WordPress core's wrapper around **CodeMirror 5** shipped since WP 4.9. **Zero new vendor files.** **`CodeEditor::maybe_prime_code_editor()`** hooks **`admin_enqueue_scripts`** at priority **`9`** and calls **`wp_enqueue_code_editor()`** once per unique mode registered for the current screen so only the modes / addons in use are loaded. The helper **`sto-code-editor.js`** declares the WP-registered handle **`code-editor`** as a dep — never bypass that.
- **Register keys:** **`section_slug`**, **`id`**, optional **`title`**, **`description`**, **`default`** (string), **`placeholder`**, **`mode`** (one of **`auto`** — auto-detect from content / **`text`** (raw fallback default) / **`css`** / **`html`** / **`javascript`** with aliases `js` / `jsx` / `ts` / **`php`** / **`json`** / **`markdown`** with alias `md` / **`xml`** / **`yaml`** with alias `yml`), **`height`** (px, default **240**, clamped **80–2000**), **`min_height`** (px, default **160**), **`line_numbers`** (bool, default **true**), **`line_wrapping`** (bool, default **false** — code stays scrollable horizontally), **`indent_size`** (1–8, default **4**), **`tab_size`** (1–8, inherits `indent_size`), **`fullscreen`** (bool, default **true** — chrome shows the expand chip), **`autocomplete`** (bool, default **true** — `Ctrl/Cmd+Space` + smart auto-trigger), **`language_switcher`** (bool, default **true** — chrome-bar `<select>` for runtime language override), **`responsive`**, **`device`**, **`wrapper_class`**, **`required`**, **`group`**, **`tooltip`**, **`tooltip_image`**, **`tooltip_preloader`**.
- **UI contract:** `FieldTitle` heading (title + tooltip + optional responsive toolbar) → soft-chrome **`.sto-code-editor`** wrapper (token-driven border / focus halo) → top **`.sto-code-editor__bar`** with either a **Select2 language switcher** (the native `.sto-code-editor__lang-select` is hidden via `visibility: hidden; position: absolute; left: -9999px` and Select2 is initialised in **`sto-code-editor.js` `initLangSelect2()`** with **`selectionCssClass: 'sto-code-editor__lang-s2'`** + **`dropdownCssClass: 'sto-code-editor__lang-dropdown'`**, **`minimumResultsForSearch: -1`**, **`width: '160px'`**, **`dropdownParent: #wpbody-content`**, and FA per-language icons rendered via **`templateSelection`** / **`templateResult`** reading **`data-sto-code-icon`** off each `<option>` — populated from **`CodeEditor::SWITCHER_MODES`** + **`CodeEditor::mode_to_icon()`** when `language_switcher => true`) or a static **`.sto-code-editor__mode-pill`** (when `language_switcher => false`), an optional **`.sto-code-editor__auto-badge`** ("Auto · CSS") that shows the heuristic's pick when `mode => 'auto'`, an optional **`.sto-code-editor__shortcut`** kbd hint (`Ctrl + Space`, hidden ≤600px), and the optional right-aligned **`.sto-code-editor__fullscreen`** chip → the **`<textarea>`** that **`wp.codeEditor.initialize()`** swaps for a CodeMirror instance. Per-field CM settings (mode, indent, line numbers, wrapping, theme, `matchBrackets`, `autoCloseBrackets`, `autoCloseTags`, `hintOptions`) are serialised as JSON in **`data-sto-code-settings`** and merged on top of WP's localized defaults inside **`sto-code-editor.js`**.
- **Switcher Select2 carve-out:** the language `<select>` deliberately **does not** carry the standard **`sto-input-select`** class — the global **`refreshStoSelect2`** loop in `main.js` would otherwise grab it and apply full-row (40 px height, 100% width) Select2 chrome that's too heavy for the compact chrome-bar pill. The dedicated init in **`initLangSelect2()`** keeps the pill at **26 px × 160 px** with **999 px radius**. CSS overrides under **`.sto-option-panel-wrapper .sto-field-row-code-editor .sto-code-editor__bar .select2-container.sto-code-editor__lang-s2 …`** carry 3 panel-wrapper-scoped classes so they beat the global `!important` rules in `sto-select2.css`. **`Assets.php`** lists **`sto-select2`** as a CSS dep and **`sto-select2-vendor`** as a JS dep so **`$.fn.select2`** is guaranteed before init runs. Falls back to the hidden native select if Select2 isn't available.
- **Auto-detect (`mode => 'auto'`):** the field starts in **`text/plain`** parser; **`detectLanguage()`** in `sto-code-editor.js` runs on mount and on every `change` event (debounced **250 ms**) and calls **`cm.setOption('mode', mime)`** with the detected mime. Detection order: PHP → HTML → XML → JSON (with `JSON.parse()` round-trip) → CSS → JavaScript → Markdown → YAML → text. **`maybe_prime_code_editor()`** primes every entry in **`CodeEditor::AUTO_PRELOAD_MIMES`** via **`wp_enqueue_code_editor()`** when any registered field uses `mode => 'auto'` or exposes the switcher (so a runtime mode switch is zero-latency). Selecting **Auto-detect** in the switcher re-arms the heuristic; selecting a concrete language disarms it. **Never** call `cm.setOption('mode', …)` from outside `sto-code-editor.js` — the auto-detect handler owns that state.
- **Autocomplete:** when `autocomplete => true` (default), the JS helper binds **`Ctrl + Space`** / **`Cmd + Space`** (`extraKeys.Ctrl-Space` / `Cmd-Space` → `instance.showHint(…)`) AND attaches a smart auto-trigger on the CodeMirror **`inputRead`** event (alpha word chars universally + context openers `<` / `.` / `@` / `:` / `$`). Hint provider is chosen per-mode by **`pickHintFn()`**: prefers **`CodeMirror.hint.css`** / **`html`** / **`javascript`** / **`xml`** / **`sql`** when the addon is present, and **always** falls back to **`CodeMirror.hint.anyword`** so plain-text / unsupported modes still get word completion against the buffer. The popup is portaled to `<body>` by CodeMirror — its **`.CodeMirror-hints`** rules therefore live at the top level of `sto-code-editor.css` (the only top-level rules in that file; everything else is scoped under `.sto-field-row-code-editor`). **`hintOptions = { completeSingle: false, closeOnUnfocus: true }`** is configured PHP-side so the popup never auto-inserts and closes when the editor loses focus.
- **Color theme:** VS Code Light-inspired token palette scoped to **`.sto-field-row-code-editor .CodeMirror .cm-*`** — `cm-keyword` blue, `cm-atom` `#0070c1`, `cm-number` green, `cm-string` red, `cm-comment` green italic, `cm-variable` `#001080`, `cm-def` `#795e26`, `cm-property` `#001080`, `cm-tag` `#800000`, `cm-attribute` `#e50000`, `cm-bracket` / `cm-operator` neutral, `cm-error` / `cm-invalidchar` red on red tint. Never restyle these tokens outside this file — other WP CodeMirror surfaces (Customizer additional CSS, plugin / theme file editor) must keep WordPress's default skin.
- **Fullscreen:** expand-chip click toggles **`.sto-code-editor--is-fullscreen`** on the wrapper and **`body.sto-code-editor-fullscreen-lock`** (overlay starts below the WP admin bar — adjusted to **46px** at **`@media (max-width: 782px)`** for the taller mobile admin bar). **Escape** exits fullscreen when focus is inside the editor. The expand / compress icons live as preset siblings (**`fa-expand`** / **`fa-compress`**) and CSS toggles their visibility via the wrapper class — never inject icons from JS.
- **Save / sanitize (`CodeEditor::sanitize_stored_value`):** every mode strips null bytes, normalises **CRLF → LF**, and hard-caps payloads at **64KB**. **`html`** runs **`wp_kses_post()`** (after `wp_unslash`) so editor-cap users can't smuggle XSS. **`json`** validates via **`json_decode()`** and re-encodes with **`JSON_PRETTY_PRINT | JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES | JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE`** — invalid input falls back to the registered **`default`** (or empty). **`css` / `javascript` / `php` / `markdown` / `xml` / `yaml` / `text`** are stored verbatim — the entire `Menu::maybe_handle_save_request()` is already gated on **`current_user_can( 'manage_options' )`**, so this is admin-only by design.
- **Conditional `required`:** **`getOptionFieldValue`** reads the textarea string. Use string equality / regex on small `text` / `json` snippets; for CSS / JS, prefer toggling visibility from a sibling switcher (free-form text rarely makes for a clean predicate).
- **Hook priority `19.55`** — between **Input** (**`19.5`**) and **Typography** (**`20`**). **`Menu::maybe_handle_save_request()`** routes posted values through **`CodeEditor::sanitize_posted_value()`**; **`get_registered_option_keys_for_leaf_section()`** adds **`CodeEditor::get_field_ids_for_section()`** to the section key registry; global search index includes **`CodeEditor::get_all_fields_for_search()`**.
- **JS:** **`sto-code-editor.js`** (handle **`sto-code-editor`**, deps on **`jquery`** + **`code-editor`** + **`display-section-on-menu`**) exposes **`window.stoInitCodeEditors( $scope )`** — called from **`refreshStoSelect2`** and the **`initStoResponsiveTabs`** flow alongside the other re-init hooks. CodeMirror needs **`cm.refresh()`** after a previously-hidden section / responsive pane becomes visible (scroll math sits at `0` until then). On every CM **`change`** the buffer is mirrored back into the underlying **`<textarea>`**; a **`submit`** listener on **`#sto-theme-settings-options-form` / `form.sto-options-form`** fires **`syncAllToTextareas()`** as a safety net before WP serializes the form. If **`wp.codeEditor`** is unavailable (user disabled syntax highlighting in their profile, or the requested mode failed to enqueue), the raw `<textarea>` stays in place with monospaced font and the chrome bar continues to work — both fullscreen toggle and the submit-time flush still run.
- **CSS:** handle **`sto-code-editor`** (deps on **`sto-style`**) scopes every override to **`.sto-field-row-code-editor`** so it cannot bleed into Customizer Additional CSS or the plugin / theme file editor (both also use `wp.codeEditor`). CodeMirror skin tweaks (gutter, cursor, selection, active-line, matching bracket) all live behind that prefix.
- **Mime mapping (for `wp_enqueue_code_editor()`):** `css` → `text/css`, `html` → `text/html`, `javascript` → `application/javascript`, `php` → `application/x-httpd-php`, `json` → `application/json`, `markdown` → `text/x-markdown`, `xml` → `text/xml`, `yaml` → `text/x-yaml`, `text` → `text/plain`, **`auto`** → `text/plain` initially, the JS detector flips it. Mapping lives in **`CodeEditor::mode_to_cm_mime()`** — extend there + **`ALLOWED_MODES`** + **`SWITCHER_MODES`** + **`AUTO_PRELOAD_MIMES`** + **`MODE_ALIASES`** + the **`mode_to_label()`** lookup in lockstep when adding new modes. The matching JS mirror lives in **`mimeForMode()`** / **`labelForMode()`** inside `sto-code-editor.js` — keep both sides in sync.
- **Carve-out — Tabs inner type:** **Code editor is not (yet) registrable as an inner field inside `Tabs`** (`type` => `tabs`). The compound composition would require an inner-type branch in **`Tabs::register_inner_clone()`**. Standalone + **Group** inner are fully wired (responsive + device + save). Add the Tabs branch + this carve-out removal in the same change if the need arises.
- **Sample:** standalone **Custom CSS / JS / HTML snippet** (`mode => 'auto'`, 320px tall — paste any snippet to demo the heuristic) + grouped **Custom code snippets** with **Header HTML** + **Footer JavaScript** side-by-side at `width => '1-2'` in **`Sample/Fields/General/General.php`** (section **Layout**).

