- When adding a feature or changing behavior, update **`README.md`** at the plugin root (Fix notes / relevant section).
- When the change alters **conventions, contracts, or “how agents should work”** on this plugin, update **this file** (`.cursor/rules/simple-theme-options.mdc`) **and** its outer twin (one folder above `wp-content/`) in the same change — from **any** Cursor tab or prompt — see **Mandatory agent checklist** §2.
- **Developer guide (HTML):** the bundle at **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/`** (`instructions.html`, `instructions-layout-wc.css`, `sto-instructions-preview-templates.html`, `rebuild-instructions-layout.mjs`) is a standalone reference (WooCommerce-style layout: nested left nav, centre prose, **PHP-only** right column with samples). Update it alongside **`README.md`** and **this file** whenever those topics change — see checklist §2. **Rebuild tool:** **`rebuild-instructions-layout.mjs`** migrates a **legacy** `instructions.html` (must contain **`#instr-preview-templates`** and **`<pre data-instr-preview="…">`** in `<main>`) into the right column, injects **PHP →** jumps, splices **`sto-instructions-preview-templates.html`** for live-preview templates, and refreshes embedded CSS from **`instructions-layout-wc.css`**. The checked-in WC layout file is **not** valid rebuild input (script exits with an error). **Manual path:** edit those four files together under **`../../docs/simple-theme-options/`**; keep the `<style>` block in **`instructions.html`** in sync with **`instructions-layout-wc.css`** when you do not run the rebuild.

## Quick search (header)

- Markup in `Options\Menu::get_section_markup()` (`.sto-quick-search` → **`.sto-quick-search-field`** wraps icon column + input so admin CSS cannot collapse left padding). Items built in **`Menu::get_search_items()`** from leaf sections, **`Group::get_groups_for_search()`**, and field lists (**`Select`**, **`ImageSelect`**, **`Switcher`**, **`Color`**, **`Input`**, **`Typography`**).
- JS: `assets/admin/js/main.js` reads **`simple_theme_options.sto_search`** (`items`, `admin_base`, `page`, `max_results`). Uses **`window.stoSyncThemeSettings`** (same as sidebar SPA navigation).
- Extend index: **`sto_search_items`** filter in `Menu::get_search_items()`.
- Scroll targets: wrapper **`id="sto-field-{field_id}"`**, group **`id="sto-group-{group_id}"`**.
- **Keyboard navigation:** **`initStoQuickSearch()`** tracks **`activeIdx`** and binds **`ArrowDown`** / **`ArrowUp`** (wrap-around), **`Home`** / **`End`**, **`Enter`** (activate), **`Escape`** (close). Active row paints via **`.sto-quick-search-item.sto-quick-search-item--active`** (`#e7f1f9` background + 3 px `#2271b1` left accent via `box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0`); `mouseenter` mirrors hover into `activeIdx` so Enter activates whatever the mouse last touched. **`aria-activedescendant`** on the input + per-option **`id="sto-quick-search-item-{idx}"`** + **`aria-selected`** mirror the active class — keep these in sync if you swap renderers. Focus must stay on the input throughout (never call `$btn.focus()` from keyboard nav — that breaks the arrow loop).
- **Landed-row flash:** activation flow lives in **`activateItem($btn)`** (shared by click + Enter). After **`scrollIntoView`** the helper **`flashField($target)`** adds **`.sto-field-flash`** (CSS keyframe **`stoFieldFlash`**, 1.6 s ease-out — soft blue halo + 14% background tint that decays), force-flushes via `offsetWidth` read so re-flashing the same row restarts the animation, and removes the class after 1700 ms via a `flashToken` closure-guarded timer. The keyframe degrades to a static 0.6 s fade under **`@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`**. Both **`.sto-field-row`** (standalone + group-inner) and **`.sto-field-group`** (group container) can carry the class — the flash rule sits at the bottom of `style.css` with `border-radius: 8px` + `position: relative` so it stacks above sibling separators.

